version: "0.4.0-draft"
date-released: 2026-10-07
year: 2026
abstract: >-
  A recursive inquiry framework for exposing how representations, conclusions,
  support, beliefs, values, evaluators, measurements, interpretations, inferences,
  assumptions, transformations, selections, boundaries, and revisions are produced and related. Recursive Truth Exposure identifies
  conclusions presently best supported as true under represented observations,
  relations, methods, measurements, and conditions without certifying identity
  with definitive truth. The framework includes applications to epistemic
  representation integrity under recursive inference, epistemic alignment, and
  recursive AI systems.
license: CC-BY-4.0
